<!--
  Recorded breaks against the published 1.0.0 baseline. Koan 1.x is the STABILIZATION line: a break inside it is
  expected, and the rule is that it must be written down rather than prevented. Everything here is a public
  surface this cycle removed or reshaped deliberately — the schema orchestrator becoming a single owner, the
  vector adapter surface, and one type that moved assemblies so a document store could reach the contract that
  governs it.

  A suppression is a record of debt, not permission to take more. Before adding one, check the removal is
  actually intended; when the line moves to 1.1 or 2.0, this file is deleted rather than carried, and
  KoanTrainBaselineVersion in Directory.Build.targets advances to the last fully published version.

  Regenerate after an intended break:
      dotnet pack Koan.sln -c Debug -p:ApiCompatGenerateSuppressionFile=true

  The gate runs at pack time only — `dotnet build` cannot see it — so a removed public member leaves a green
  solution and an unshippable package. See docs/engineering/nuget-publishing.md.
-->
